Dropped by watermark per stateful operator: {'stateStoreSave': 0, 'dedupeWithinWatermark': 186}

Spark only guarantees one direction: rows within the watermark delay are never dropped; rows later
than it MAY be dropped. The watermark a micro-batch filters with comes from earlier batches, so when the
consumer lags and one batch spans more event time than the delay, late rows in that batch get through.

